ecision constraints [AXIOM]. Reopen if: any handoff lacks version acknowledgment of recovery-candidate, affected-lot, or assay-plan; if quality-unit release decision is substituted by other roles; if emergency purchasing waives validated controls.\n\n## SOURCE BRAMBLE\nVERSION b5887292924f964689a1d92f2f9d7592183070bd5501148d5be30f58aa1619d4\n\n### REQUIREMENTS\nQ02: Defines hazard thresholds, lot/line holds, investigation triggers, and release rules. Q11: Specifies sampling context for M41 samples and assay-drift probability interpretation. Q12: Requires preservation of exact units and meanings for thresholds, observed values, and probabilities.\n\n### FINDINGS\nAlert threshold: 0.25 EU/mL; rejection limit: 0.50 EU/mL [BRAMBLE]. Two validated M41 samples measured 0.31 and 0.34 EU/mL; lot remains held during open water-loop investigation despite values below rejection limit [BRAMBLE]. Stability modeling assigns 41 percent probability of assay drift after eighteen hours; this is not humidity, defect prevalence, or readiness score [BRAMBLE]. Operational evidence (QUAL-000 to QUAL-047) spans lot-M41, line-A, line-B, water-loop across revisions r2-r4. Hold status appears in QUAL-000 (lot-M41, 0.2 EU/mL), QUAL-013 (line-A, 3.1 EU/mL), QUAL-026 (line-B, 3.0 EU/mL), QUAL-039 (water-loop, 2.8 EU/mL) [BRAMBLE].\n\n### QUALIFICATIONS AND CONFLICTS\nValues and units must not be converted into hours, percent, or temperature [BRAMBLE]. HEATH defines valid confirmation/release rounds; DRIFT and EMBER changes invalidate prior line samples for changed candidates [BRAMBLE]. NORTH identified prior mismatched lot revisions in particulate/endotoxin reporting [BRAMBLE]. No internal conflicts; thresholds remain distinct from observed values.\n\n### UNKNOWNS AND REOPEN CONDITIONS\nUnspecified: exact mechanism linking 41% drift probability to hold duration; specific conditions starting, holding, expanding, or retiring lot/line controls per decision constraints [BRAMBLE]. Reopen if: any water-loop investigation finding changes; if DRIFT or EMBER candidate versions change; if M41 sample values approach rejection limit (0.50 EU/mL); if HEATH confirmation rounds are invalidated."}
